## Red Flags

These thoughts mean STOP—you're rationalizing:

| Thought | Reality |
|---------|---------|
| "This is just a simple question" | Questions are tasks. Check for skills. |
| "I need more context first" | Skill check comes BEFORE clarifying questions. |
| "Let me explore the codebase first" | Skills tell you HOW to explore. Check first. |
| "I can check git/files quickly" | Files lack conversation context. Check for skills. |
| "Let me gather information first" | Skills tell you HOW to gather information. |
| "This doesn't need a formal skill" | If a skill exists, use it. |
| "I remember this skill" | Skills evolve. Read current version. |
| "This doesn't count as a task" | Action = task. Check for skills. |
| "The skill is overkill" | Simple things become complex. Use it. |
| "I'll just do this one thing first" | Check BEFORE doing anything. |
| "This feels productive" | Undisciplined action wastes time. Skills prevent this. |
| "I know what that means" | Knowing the concept ≠ using the skill. Invoke it. |

## Skill Priority

When multiple skills could apply, use this order:

1. **Process skills first** (brainstorming, debugging) - these determine HOW to approach the task
2. **Implementation skills second** (frontend-design, mcp-builder) - these guide execution

"Let's build X" → brainstorming first, then implementation skills.
"Fix this bug" → debugging first, then domain-specific skills.

## Skill Types

**Rigid** (TDD, debugging): Follow exactly. Don't adapt away discipline.

**Flexible** (patterns): Adapt principles to context.

The skill itself tells you which.

## User Instructions

Instructions say WHAT, not HOW. "Add X" or "Fix Y" doesn't mean skip workflows.
# BizCity Twin AI — Workspace Map

CLASS: MAP · Last updated: 2026-08-26

BizCity Twin AI is a self-hosted, WordPress-native business Second Brain
that combines Graph RAG, memory, CRM, communication channels, and
automation. Server-side `bizcity-llm-router` questions belong in that
separate repository; this repository owns the WordPress client framework
and its bundled extensions. **CONTEXT.md** (next to this file) routes
tasks to the right workspace. This file is the map.

## Folder Structure

```
bizcity-twin-ai/
├── CLAUDE.md            ← the map (always loaded)
├── CONTEXT.md           ← the router: task → workspace
├── AGENTS.md            ← cross-vendor shim (Codex etc.)
├── bizcity-twin-ai.php  ← plugin entry point / bootstrap
├── bin/                 ← repository validators and CLI utilities
├── core/                ← shared WordPress AI framework subsystems
├── docs/                ← guides, contracts, audits, runbooks, laws.md
├── examples/            ← public SDK reference-plugin fixture
├── includes/            ← top-level WordPress bootstrap support
├── languages/           ← localization catalogs
├── modules/             ← first-party feature modules (twin*/webchat)
├── mu-plugin/           ← WordPress must-use plugin integration
├── packages/            ← standalone framework SDK packages
├── plugins/             ← first-party WordPress feature plugins
├── tests/               ← unit, MCP, and fixture test material
└── tools/               ← repository maintenance utilities
```

`.github/` carries CI, DCO, release workflows, and repository
collaboration metadata.

## Quick Navigation

| Want to… | Go here |
|---|---|
| Route a task / know what to load | `CONTEXT.md` |
| Work on a core subsystem | `core/CONTEXT.md` |
| Work on a feature module | `modules/CONTEXT.md` |
| Work on a bundled plugin | `plugins/CONTEXT.md` |
| Pipeline orchestration architecture | `core/intent/docs/PIPELINE-ARCHITECTURE.md` |
| Framework ownership / public contracts | `docs/framework/FRAMEWORK-GUIDE-v1.md` |
| Repository boundary & contribution rules | `CONTRIBUTING.md` |
| Exclusions and STOP rules | `docs/laws.md` |

## Naming & Placement

Derived from this repository's own conventions — follow the cited
examples when creating a NEW file:

| New body | Place and pattern | Existing examples |
|---|---|---|
| PHP class | `<area>/includes/class-<name>.php` | `includes/class-module-loader.php`, `core/memory/includes/class-memory-manager.php` |
| Core subsystem | `core/<subsystem>/` | `core/memory/`, `core/diagnostics/` |
| Feature module | `modules/<name>/` with `module.json` | `modules/webchat/module.json` |
| Feature plugin | `plugins/bizcity-<name>/` | `plugins/bizcity-doc/`, `plugins/bizcity-tool-image/` |
| Diagnostics probe | `core/diagnostics/includes/probes/class-probe-<topic>.php` | `class-probe-twinweb-customer-channels.php` |
| Test | `tests/unit/` or `tests/mcp/`; fixtures in `tests/fixtures/` | `tests/bootstrap.php` |
| Documentation | `docs/<area>/` descriptive name | `docs/framework/FRAMEWORK-GUIDE-v1.md` |
| Translation | `languages/bizcity-twin-ai-<locale>.po` | `languages/bizcity-twin-ai-vi.po` |
| Repo validator | `bin/` | `bin/bizcity-manifest-validate.php` |

Automated PHP style enforcement is configured in `phpcs.xml.dist`, and
repository CI entry points live in `.github/workflows/ci.yml`; those
files remain the authority for machine-enforced checks.

Excluded from reading (full reasons: `docs/laws.md`): `.git/`,
`.worktrees/`, `vendor/`, `node_modules/`, generated outputs, runtime
logs, `tests/_archived/`.
# BizCity Twin AI — Task Router

**CLAUDE.md** (always loaded) has the folder map and naming rules.
This file routes you to work. Read the target workspace's CONTEXT.md,
load only what it names, and skip everything else.

## Task Routing

| Your Task | Go Here | You'll Also Need |
|---|---|---|
| Change a core subsystem (memory, knowledge, intent, diagnostics…) | `core/CONTEXT.md` | `core/twin-core/` if public contracts are touched |
| Fix a diagnostics probe or fixture | `core/CONTEXT.md` → `core/diagnostics/` | `tests/fixtures/` for probe evidence |
| Change a feature module (twinchat, twinweb, webchat…) | `modules/CONTEXT.md` | `includes/class-module-loader.php` for load order |
| Change a bundled plugin (CRM, content, image, Zalo…) | `plugins/CONTEXT.md` | `docs/framework/FRAMEWORK-GUIDE-v1.md` for ownership boundaries |
| Add a sample/reference plugin per the Twin AI agent standard | `plugins/CONTEXT.md` | `examples/CONTEXT.md` for the public-contract fixture |
| Change plugin bootstrap or module loading | root `bizcity-twin-ai.php` | `includes/CONTEXT.md` |
| Change an SDK package | `packages/CONTEXT.md` | `bin/validate-sdk-release.mjs` |
| Write or fix tests | `tests/CONTEXT.md` | the subsystem under test only |
| Write documentation | `docs/CONTEXT.md` | — |
| Update translations | `languages/CONTEXT.md` | — |
| Run validators / repo maintenance | `bin/CONTEXT.md` | `tools/CONTEXT.md` |

## Workspace Summary

| Workspace | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `bin/` | repository validators and command-line utilities |
| `core/` | shared WordPress AI framework subsystems (25 areas) |
| `docs/` | guides, contracts, audits, runbooks, reference material |
| `examples/` | public SDK reference-plugin fixture |
| `includes/` | top-level WordPress bootstrap support |
| `languages/` | localization catalogs |
| `modules/` | first-party feature modules |
| `mu-plugin/` | WordPress must-use plugin integration |
| `packages/` | standalone framework SDK packages (PHP + TypeScript) |
| `plugins/` | first-party WordPress feature plugins |
| `tests/` | unit, MCP, fixture, and archived test material |
| `tools/` | repository maintenance utilities |

## Cross-Workspace Flow

```
bizcity-twin-ai.php → includes/ (bootstrap, module loader) → modules/
core/twin-core (public contracts + event stream)
    → implemented by modules/ and plugins/
    → distributed externally via packages/ SDKs
    → demonstrated by examples/bizcity-reference-plugin
    → validated by bin/ (manifest, contract, event-stream validators)
```

Before public disclosure, contract bypass, or server-side work:
read the STOP rules in `docs/laws.md`.

