# Laws — STOP rules and exclusions

CLASS: LAWS · Last updated: 2026-08-26

## Universal STOP rules

- STOP before publicly disclosing a suspected vulnerability because
  coordinated disclosure protects users; follow `SECURITY.md` for the
  full reporting policy.
- STOP before bypassing a framework ownership or public-contract
  boundary because parallel implementations cause drift; follow
  `docs/framework/FRAMEWORK-GUIDE-v1.md` for the full workflow.
- STOP before implementing server-only `bizcity-llm-router` behavior
  here because this is the WordPress client repository; follow
  `CONTRIBUTING.md` for the repository boundary and contribution rules.

## Explicit exclusions

- `.git/` is repository metadata, so agents do not treat its internals
  as product context.
- `.worktrees/` and harness-managed worktree directories are execution
  infrastructure, so they are not product areas.
- `vendor/` and `node_modules/` are third-party dependency caches, so
  their generated contents are not repository knowledge.
- `dist/`, `build/`, `coverage/`, and `.cache/` are generated outputs
  or caches, so their source directories remain the authority.
- `plugins/bizcity-facebook-bot/logs/`, `error_log`, and other runtime
  logs are operational output, so they are not context sources.
- `tests/_archived/` is historical test material, so current test
  behavior is owned by the active test directories.

An unlisted directory is a gap in this layer, not an ignorable area.
# core/ — shared WordPress AI framework subsystems

Every subsystem lives in its own directory; PHP classes sit in that
subsystem's `includes/` as `class-<name>.php`. Public contracts and the
canonical event stream live in `core/twin-core` — cross-subsystem work
goes through them, never around them.

## Subsystems

| Subsystem | Path | What it owns |
|---|---|---|
| agent runtime | `core/agents` | agent bootstrap and contracts |
| automation | `core/automation` | workflow automation runtime |
| LLM client | `core/bizcity-llm` | client-side LLM integration and documentation |
| marketplace | `core/bizcity-market` | marketplace assets, libraries, and templates |
| channel gateway | `core/channel-gateway` | multi-channel integration and inbox gateway |
| content operations | `core/content-ops` | shared content operations |
| cron | `core/cron` | scheduled execution support |
| diagnostics | `core/diagnostics` | diagnostic probes and schema changelog evidence |
| helpers | `core/helper` | current shared helpers and UX contracts |
| legacy helpers | `core/helper-legacy` | legacy helper flows retained for compatibility |
| intent engine | `core/intent` | intent planning, orchestration, and pipeline architecture |
| knowledge | `core/knowledge` | knowledge base, KG Hub, and retrieval services |
| MCP | `core/mcp` | Model Context Protocol integration and REST surfaces |
| membership | `core/membership` | membership behavior and templates |
| memory | `core/memory` | persistent memory, migrations, and views |
| persona | `core/persona` | persona runtime |
| research | `core/research` | research providers and interfaces |
| runtime | `core/runtime` | shared runtime wiring |
| scheduler | `core/scheduler` | scheduling runtime and views |
| skills | `core/skills` | skill library and skill-management UI |
| SMTP | `core/smtp` | mail transport integration |
| tools | `core/tools` | built-in content, distribution, planning, scheduling, video, and workspace tools |
| Twin core | `core/twin-core` | public contracts and the canonical event stream |
| TwinBrain | `core/twinbrain` | assistant runtime and tools |
| core TwinSearch | `core/twinsearch` | shared TwinSearch backend integration |

## What to Load

| Task shape | Load these | Skip these |
|---|---|---|
| Change one subsystem | that subsystem's dir only | all sibling subsystems |
| Fix a diagnostics probe | `core/diagnostics/includes/probes/` | other subsystems; pull `tests/fixtures/` only for evidence |
| Touch public contracts | the subsystem + `core/twin-core` | UI-only areas |
| Pipeline/orchestration design | `core/intent/docs/PIPELINE-ARCHITECTURE.md` (single home for plan schema, executor design, lifecycle, integration, async support, rollout record) | unrelated subsystems |

## Inputs / Outputs

- Input: module/plugin feature needs arriving through `core/twin-core`
  contracts.
- Output: shared services consumed by `modules/`, `plugins/`, and the
  SDKs in `packages/`.
